# (BERLIN, the Lead's memory, spec 3.5 and 7.3) the white keys write the theme: Timewind (D Aeolian, 96 BPM: a
# sixteenth 156 ms) in Emerge, its long intro, the generated Lead silent. Four white keys in a bar, a quarter each
# (w4 w5 w3 w2: A4 Bb4 G4 F4); two beats after the last is let go the figure is the theme, and at the next bar line the
# Lead plays it back as it was played: its call (the last note its open ending's), then after a beat or two its answer
# (the same, the last note closed and held twice as long)
wait 300
expect pool 1453
bar 2
peakreset
key w4 down
wait 620
key w4 up
key w5 down
wait 620
key w5 up
key w3 down
wait 620
key w3 up
key w2 down
wait 620
key w2 up
expect notes_ch3 4
expect lastnote_ch3 65
# the call, from bar 4's downbeat: A4, Bb4, G4, then its ending
bar 4
wait 300
expect lastnote_ch3 69
wait 625
expect lastnote_ch3 70
wait 625
expect lastnote_ch3 67
wait 625
expect notes_ch3 8
# the answer, after a breath of two beats (calm): the same, from A4 again
wait 1900
expect notes_ch3 9
expect lastnote_ch3 69
wait 625
expect lastnote_ch3 70
wait 625
expect lastnote_ch3 67
wait 3000
expect notes_ch3 12
